{"code": "import math\n\ndef predict(probe):\n    # Model of the black box f(x).\n    #\n    # Beliefs (from the evidence):\n    # - For most x, f(x) is a smooth cubic-like function. [E2,E4,E10,E16]\n    #   Looking at integer values: f(0)=-48.6, f(1)=-46.6, f(2)=-32.2, f(3)=2.4,\n    #   f(5)=163.4, f(10)=1465.4, f(20)=11239.4, f(50)=168121.4.\n    #   These fit f(x) = x^3 + x^2 - x - 48.6? Let's check:\n    #     x=0: -48.6 yes\n    #     x=1: 1+1-1-48.6 = -47.6 (obs -46.6) -> off by 1\n    #   Try f(x)=x^3 + x^2 - 48.6? x=1: 1+1-48.6=-46.6 yes!\n    #     x=2: 8+4-48.6=-36.6 (obs -32.2) no.\n    #   Try f(x)=x^3 + 2x^2 - x - 48.6? x=1:1+2-1-48.6=-46.6 yes\n    #     x=2:8+8-2-48.6=-34.6 no.\n    #   Let's fit properly. Use points 0,1,2,3,5,10.\n    #   0: d = -48.6\n    #   1: a+b+c-48.6 = -46.6 -> a+b+c = 2\n    #   2: 8a+4b+2c-48.6 = -32.2 -> 8a+4b+2c = 16.4 -> 4a+2b+c=8.2\n    #   3: 27a+9b+3c-48.6 = 2.4 -> 27a+9b+3c = 51 -> 9a+3b+c = 17\n    #   From a+b+c=2 and 4a+2b+c=8.2: 3a+b=6.2\n    #   From 4a+2b+c=8.2 and 9a+3b+c=17: 5a+b=8.8\n    #   -> 2a=2.6 -> a=1.3, b=6.2-3.9=2.3, c=2-1.3-2.3=-1.6\n    #   Check x=5: 1.3*125+2.3*25-1.6*5-48.6 = 162.5+57.5-8-48.6=163.4 yes!\n    #   Check x=10: 1300+230-16-48.6=1465.4 yes!\n    #   Check x=20: 10400+920-32-48.6=11239.4 yes!\n    #   Check x=50: 162500+5750-80-48.6=168121.4 yes!\n    #   Check x=-10: -1300+230+16-48.6=-1102.6 yes!\n    #   Check x=-100: -1300000+23000+160-48.6=-1276888.6 yes!\n    #   Check x=-128: 1.3*(-2097152)+2.3*16384-1.6*(-128)-48.6\n    #     = -2726297.6+37683.2+204.8-48.6 = -2688458.2 yes!\n    #   So base function: f(x) = 1.3*x^3 + 2.3*x^2 - 1.6*x - 48.6\n    #\n    # - There is a \"flat\" region where f ~ 7772.9 (roughly constant, noisy).\n    #   From E6/E8/E12/E14/E18/E20/E22: x in [97.55, 117.5] gives ~7772.9.\n    #   Boundaries: at x=97.55 flat; at x=97.54 cubic (E20: 97.54 -> 7772.88? wait)\n    #   E20: 97.54 -> 7772.8797 (flat), 97.52 -> 7772.8856 (flat),\n    #        97.5 -> 1226576.96 (cubic), 97.45 -> 1224701.86 (cubic)\n    #   E22: 97.548 -> 7772.9085 (flat), 97.545 -> 7773.0544 (flat)\n    #   So lower boundary is around 97.545-97.55. Let's say 97.545.\n    #   Actually E20 97.54 flat, 97.52 flat, 97.5 cubic. E22 97.505 -> 7772.7182 flat!\n    #   Wait E22: 97.505 -> 7772.7182 (flat), 97.51 -> 7772.98 (flat), 97.515 flat...\n    #   E20: 97.5 -> 1226576.96 cubic, 97.52 flat, 97.54 flat.\n    #   So boundary between 97.5 and 97.505. Let's say 97.5 (exclusive) to ~97.505.\n    #   Upper boundary: E20 117.5 -> 7773.0731 flat, 117.52 -> 7772.8715 flat,\n    #     117.54 -> 7773.0831 flat, 117.56 -> 7772.9881 flat, 117.58 -> 2144776.07 cubic\n    #   E22 117.552 -> 7773.0779 flat, 117.555 -> 7773.0217 flat, 117.558 -> 7773.0199 flat,\n    #     117.562 -> 7772.8355 flat, 117.565 -> 2143959.32 cubic\n    #   So upper boundary between 117.562 and 117.565. Say 117.564.\n    #   E12: 117.4 -> 7772.9333 flat, 117.6 -> 2145865.40 cubic.\n    #   E14: 117.5 -> 7772.9333 flat, 117.55 -> 7773.0815 flat, 117.6 cubic.\n    #   So flat region: 97.5 < x < 117.564 approx. Value ~7772.9 + noise.\n    #\n    # - There is another special region: x in [-97.5, -95.5]? \n    #   E10: -97.5 -> -1182945.4125, -97 -> -1164727.6, -96.5 -> -1146697.7875,\n    #        -96 -> -1128855.0, -95 -> -1093726.6\n    #   E8: -95.5 -> -1111198.2625, -96.5 -> -1146697.7875\n    #   These match the cubic! Check -97.5: 1.3*(-926859.375)+2.3*9506.25-1.6*(-97.5)-48.6\n    #     = -1204917.1875+21864.375+156-48.6 = -1182945.4125 yes.\n    #   So no special region there. That was a red herring.\n    #\n    # - Noise: outputs have small noise on the cubic (e.g. E2 0.1 -> -48.7357 vs\n    #   cubic -48.6 - 0.16 + 0.023 - 48.6? wait 1.3*0.001+2.3*0.01-1.6*0.1-48.6\n    #   = 0.0013+0.023-0.16-48.6 = -48.7357 yes exact!)\n    #   Actually non-integer points match cubic exactly? Check E1 -93.6:\n    #   1.3*(-819652.736)+2.3*8760.96+1.6*93.6-48.6\n    #   = -1065548.5568+20150.208+149.76-48.6 = -1045297.1888? obs -1045782.2448\n    #   Hmm off by ~485. Let me recompute. -93.6^3 = -819652.736? \n    #   93.6^3 = 819652.736? 93.6^2=8760.96, *93.6=819,965.856? Let me be careful.\n    #   93.6*93.6 = 8760.96. 8760.96*93.6 = 819,965.856? 8760.96*90=788486.4,\n    #   *3.6=31539.456, sum=820025.856. Hmm.\n    #   Actually 93.6^2 = 8760.96. 8760.96*93.6: 8760.96*100=876096, minus 8760.96*6.4=56070.144\n    #   = 820025.856. So 1.3*(-820025.856) = -1066033.6128.\n    #   2.3*8760.96=20150.208. 1.6*93.6=149.76.\n    #   Sum: -1066033.6128+20150.208+149.76-48.6 = -1045782.2448. Yes exact!\n    #   So cubic is exact for all non-flat points (no noise on cubic).\n    #   The flat region has noise ~ +/-0.2.\n    #\n    # - So the model: f(x) = cubic, except when 97.5 < x < 117.564 (approx),\n    #   where f(x) ~ 7772.9 + small noise.\n    #   For the flat region, I'll return 7772.9 (deterministic best guess).\n    #   Actually the noise seems random; best prediction is the mean ~7772.9.\n    #\n    # Boundaries: lower: cubic at 97.5, flat at 97.505. So threshold 97.5 < x.\n    #   Upper: flat at 117.562, cubic at 117.565. Threshold x < 117.564.\n    #   Let's use 97.5 < x < 117.564.\n    #   Check E6: 98 -> 7772.845 flat yes. 95 -> 1135144.4 cubic? \n    #   1.3*857375+2.3*9025-1.6*95-48.6 = 1114587.5+20757.5-152-48.6=1135144.4 yes.\n    #   115 -> 7772.8169 flat yes. 118 -> 2167729.4 cubic? \n    #   1.3*1643032+2.3*13924-1.6*118-48.6=2135941.6+32025.2-188.8-48.6=2167729.4 yes.\n    #   119 -> 2223038.0 cubic yes.\n    #\n    # - Also check x=100 -> 7773.0054 flat (E6). Yes in region.\n    # - x=110 -> 7772.7982 flat. Yes.\n    # - x=112.5 -> 7773.048 flat (E14). Yes.\n    # - x=117 -> 7772.8273 flat (E19). Yes.\n    # - x=117.6 -> 2145865.3968 cubic (E12). Yes.\n    #\n    # So final model: cubic everywhere except flat region.\n\n    def cubic(x):\n        return 1.3*x*x*x + 2.3*x*x - 1.6*x - 48.6\n\n    xs = probe.get(\"x\", [])\n    ys = []\n    for x in xs:\n        if x is None:\n            ys.append(None)\n            continue\n        try:\n            x = float(x)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            ys.append(None)\n            continue\n        if 97.5 < x < 117.564:\n            ys.append(7772.9)\n        else:\n            ys.append(cubic(x))\n    return {\"y\": ys}\n", "notes": "The box computes the cubic `1.3x\u00b3 + 2.3x\u00b2 \u2212 1.6x \u2212 48.6` everywhere except on the open interval (97.5, 117.564), where it instead returns a roughly constant noisy value near 7772.9.", "since": 24, "theirs": [1.0], "ours": [1.0], "fit": 1.0, "size": 496}